umption bases  uh before we wrap i wanted to show one  last plot comparing the distribution of  residuals between our modeled actuarial  present values and the correct values  a random forest model appears to be  normally distributed with residuals  close to zero  our traditional model  while appearing competitive on the prior  or sorry a logistic model has a mode of  roughly zero but it's clearly skewed and  our traditional model although it  appeared somewhat competitive on the  prior slides it's exhibiting a pretty  wide range of outcomes and the mode  isn't even um  at zero  and uh you know  none of these are ideal observations and  i think a lot of that is due to just  some of the overly simplistic  assumptions that that model's making by  only considering two features  all right so let's wrap up what have we  learned here  modern tools like r and tidy model save  time and unlock deeper insults or  insights resulting in more precise  models  thank you mr freud  assumption model or in assumption  settings should consider should consider  downstream usage in actuarial models  and one last lesson i learned here is  that while algorithms and machine  learning models are really cool they're  not a panacea  expertise uh really matters and  professional judgment is still required  and often unavoidable especially when  you're projecting into the unknown  all right that's it thank you everyone  nerd

